## Flight report

**Sweep (k0–4):** Turned in place from heading -180° in four 45° steps (through -140, -100, -59, -19); no gate visible until heading -19°, where a close yellow post/teal crossbar appeared near the L mark.

**Commit / crossing (k5–10):** Squared up (turn +30°, then +7° heading) and flew 2 m straight — overshot to being beside the near post (single post filling frame). Backed up 1.5 m per R5, re-squared with a 15° right turn, then a 0.8 m sideways correction (R4, "off-centre toward the near post") before crossing 2 m straight through. On the far side (x≈2.15, y≈-0.83), a small yellow post still partly blocked the view; a further 15° right turn opened a clear gap revealing a room beyond with a standing grey figure near a brick archway.

**Mannequin found:** First seen at decision **k=11** (x=2.15, y=-0.83, heading -19°), positioned near the **L mark** (left side of the forward panel), against a back wall near a shelf/archway.

**Approach (k11–13):** Turned left 22° + flew 1.84 m forward/0.77 m left toward its estimated bearing; then a second correction (turn +8°, 1.98 m forward/0.28 m left) closed most of the remaining distance, bringing the figure large and roughly centered in frame (grey body, dark top/trousers, bare feet visible — consistent with the mannequin description, not the safety pilot). Final decision (k=13) held with zero movement.

**Final pose:** x=5.78, y=-0.44, z=1.50, heading +8° (+0.14 rad), figure filling most of the panel height and roughly centered.

**Assessment:** I believe I ended close to and facing the mannequin (~1 m estimated), though the last approach leg was a size-based distance estimate rather than a measured range, so slight residual offset is possible — no further decisions were available to refine it.
